1
00:00:08,717 --> 00:00:11,803
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:29,904
[Vicki] We're here! We're here!
[chuckles]

3
00:00:29,988 --> 00:00:31,322
[Ken] Took you long enough.

4
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:33,867
Oh, you know, your dad. [laughs]

5
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:37,370
Well, Kelly and I set up everything.
We did the tables and chairs.

6
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:38,455
So, y'all can relax.

7
00:00:38,538 --> 00:00:39,831
You should've told us, we could've helped.

8
00:00:39,914 --> 00:00:43,752
-I told him to, but he--
-No! It's our pleasure. Who's this guy?

9
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:46,755
-Oh, wait. Is that Li'l Andy?
-Yeah, yeah.

10
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:49,257
-Li'l Drew-Drew-Bear, what's up?
-I'm here finally. What's up?

11
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:50,592
Didn't get dressed up? That's okay.

12
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:52,844
All righty then.
Oh, look, this is perfect. [chuckles]

13
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:54,429
You get the tripod I gave you guys?

14
00:00:54,512 --> 00:00:55,930
-Did you bring it?
-Oh, where's my brain?

15
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:57,974
-That's okay. I have one in the truck.
-Oh, okay.

16
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,642
-I'll take the photo.
-No, no, no.

17
00:00:59,726 --> 00:01:00,560
No, I got it.

18
00:01:00,643 --> 00:01:01,478
-Yep.
-Oh, no.

19
00:01:01,561 --> 00:01:03,521
No, you're not gonna want a photo
in a couple of years

20
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:05,440
with some random girl Gus was dating.

21
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:06,357
-All right.
-Yeah, we do.

22
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:10,528
I mean, not in that way,
but we want you, too.

23
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:11,571
Let her take it.

24
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:14,532
All right, everybody, happy 40th!

25
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:16,534
[all] Happy 40th!

26
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:19,913
-[Mickey] All right, there you go.
-You got it? Okay.

27
00:01:19,996 --> 00:01:21,748
Perfect. Good, good.

28
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:24,000
-[Ken] I'm gonna put the music on, Mom.
-Oh, thank you.

29
00:01:24,084 --> 00:01:26,711
-Now, is this what they call a disco ball?
-Yeah.

30
00:01:26,795 --> 00:01:28,755
-[Vicki] Where did you get that?
-[Ken] This is called a 40-50.

31
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:31,549
When we went into the party store...
They got 30-40. I went 40-50.

32
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:33,968
-Yeah. I, oh, wow. Thank you.
-Yeah.

33
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:35,595
-Hey.
-Jesus!

34
00:01:35,678 --> 00:01:37,430
Sorry, I knew that was gonna happen.

35
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:39,474
I was, like,
"I'm gonna scare her right here, so..."

36
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:42,101
-What? What do you want?
-Um...

37
00:01:42,977 --> 00:01:46,105
I just wanted to apologize
about last night,

38
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:48,691
-the stuff that was said.
-I'm gonna go back to LA.

39
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:49,984
What?

40
00:01:50,068 --> 00:01:52,112
I'm looking for flights
on my phone right now.

41
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:54,447
-I'm gonna fly out in a few hours.
-Come on...

42
00:01:54,531 --> 00:01:58,368
-I hope they have that good potato salad.
-Oh, they always have potato salad.

43
00:01:58,451 --> 00:02:00,912
-Gus-man! That you?
-Hey. Hi.

44
00:02:00,995 --> 00:02:03,039
We've been watching your Witchita show.

45
00:02:03,122 --> 00:02:06,084
Spooky stuff! Spooky, spooky stuff.

46
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:10,463
[chuckles] Well, I'm glad you like it.
Um... Uh...

47
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:13,216
-Sorry, this is my girlfriend Mickey.
-[man] Hello!

48
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:14,551
-This is my...
-Hi, there.

49
00:02:14,634 --> 00:02:17,971
...Uncle Pat and Aunt Jo right there.
Yeah.

50
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:26,396
So, yeah... Everybody's in there,
and I'll be in there soon.

51
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,356
All right, okay...

52
00:02:28,439 --> 00:02:30,817
-We'll see you soon.
-See you soon. Okay, bye.

53
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,402
-[Jo] Bye.
-Bye.

54
00:02:34,612 --> 00:02:36,614
[sighs] So this is what you're doing?

55
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:40,493
You're just threatening to break up
and leave now,

56
00:02:40,577 --> 00:02:42,620
because of what?
Because of a stupid fight?

57
00:02:42,704 --> 00:02:46,374
See, you still don't get it.
It wasn't stupid.

58
00:02:46,457 --> 00:02:49,961
You said I was unstable,
and you didn't see a future for us.

59
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:52,046
Okay, look...

60
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:53,631
When I heard you say that right now,

61
00:02:53,715 --> 00:02:57,302
I think maybe there has been
some sort of misunderstanding

62
00:02:57,385 --> 00:02:59,846
-or misinterpretation of what I said--
-No.

63
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:02,557
It wasn't a fucking TS Eliot poem, Gus.

64
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,976
It didn't need interpretation.
I knew what you meant.

65
00:03:05,935 --> 00:03:07,562
Look, this is very--

66
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:10,440
This is insane, okay?
We haven't ever talked about this before.

67
00:03:10,523 --> 00:03:11,441
I don't even know my...

68
00:03:11,524 --> 00:03:13,693
God damn it! Fucking shit! Hey!

69
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:15,945
-Hey, Gus!
-Hi.

70
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:17,906
-Hello.
-Who's this now?

71
00:03:17,989 --> 00:03:20,325
Oh, this is my girlfriend Mickey.

72
00:03:20,408 --> 00:03:22,952
And this is my cousin Lisa
and her family. Hi, guys.

73
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:27,040
I've already seen her all over Facebook,
so I feel like I know her already.

74
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:30,501
-Oh, yeah, sure.
-Gus, is there a TV in there?

75
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:33,630
No, I don't think there's a TV. Sorry.

76
00:03:33,713 --> 00:03:35,715
-Mom, you said there'd be a TV!
-You lied!

77
00:03:35,798 --> 00:03:37,383
No, nobody lied. Let's go.

78
00:03:38,843 --> 00:03:39,761
[Lisa] Hey!

79
00:03:39,844 --> 00:03:42,931
I gotta get outta here, 'cause I cannot
be the welcoming committee, okay?

80
00:03:43,014 --> 00:03:44,515
-I'm going back to LA.
-You can't do this.

81
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:46,392
-You can't do this to me.
-Why the fuck not?

82
00:03:46,476 --> 00:03:48,770
Because this is gonna be
fuckin' hell, okay?

83
00:03:48,853 --> 00:03:51,397
Being trapped here with my family
and pretending everything's okay,

84
00:03:51,481 --> 00:03:53,191
while you and me are falling apart?

85
00:03:54,943 --> 00:03:55,944
Please?

86
00:03:57,153 --> 00:03:58,571
Fine, I will stay for this party,

87
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:02,075
but then I am leaving afterwards,
and you can stay here until the--

88
00:04:02,158 --> 00:04:03,493
[sighs] Oh, my God.

89
00:04:03,576 --> 00:04:07,830
Can we just go in there?
'Cause I can't say hi to another person.

90
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:10,083
[Mickey sighs]

91
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:11,793
-[whispers] They gone?
-No.

92
00:04:13,419 --> 00:04:14,712
-Go.
-Okay.

93
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:17,840
They make you use their caterer

94
00:04:17,924 --> 00:04:19,259
-when you rent this place, though.
-Oh, yeah.

95
00:04:19,342 --> 00:04:21,094
It's a real sweet print, isn't it?

96
00:04:21,177 --> 00:04:23,680
-Isn't it sweet!
-This is just so tender.

97
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:26,891
The beams on Tower 7
were demolished diagonally, okay?

98
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:30,144
-When you do a regular demolition...
-Okay.

99
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:33,564
-Shall we enter the abyss?
-Mm-hmm.

100
00:04:36,651 --> 00:04:37,860
-Hello.
-Hi.

101
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:39,529
[woman] I watched your witch show.

102
00:04:39,612 --> 00:04:40,780
What'd you think?

103
00:04:40,863 --> 00:04:45,535
I mean, I could do without
the devil worshiping and the paganism.

104
00:04:45,618 --> 00:04:47,245
And then one morning, we wake up,

105
00:04:47,328 --> 00:04:49,580
and our entire world is being run
by one government.

106
00:04:50,498 --> 00:04:52,542
-Really? You think so?
-Mm-hmm

107
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:55,628
The only real obstacle
to selling recreational vehicles

108
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:57,547
is that people consider it a luxury.

109
00:04:58,131 --> 00:04:59,799
That's partly a problem with the name.

110
00:04:59,882 --> 00:05:02,844
"Recreational." So what you do is,
you convince people,

111
00:05:02,927 --> 00:05:05,430
and I was telling you this earlier,
that it's a necessary luxury.

112
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:09,267
That's how you hook 'em,
and then that's how you bring 'em in.

113
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:10,435
All right, excuse me.

114
00:05:10,935 --> 00:05:14,063
I am just so proud of all my children.

115
00:05:14,147 --> 00:05:17,984
The dealerships
and the charities and the art shows

116
00:05:18,067 --> 00:05:20,320
and the teaching...
No, Gussie, your movie.

117
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:22,905
Don't forget. That, too. [chuckles]

118
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:27,744
I'm for the creative stuff, for sure,
but there's nobility in education.

119
00:05:27,827 --> 00:05:31,581
Teachers are heroes,
like a firefighter or a soldier, I think.

120
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:32,874
Hmm.

121
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:35,835
[Ken] Okay, everybody, listen up!

122
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:41,174
First of all, let's give it up for
Mr. and Mrs. Victoria and Mark Cruikshank.

123
00:05:41,257 --> 00:05:43,801
[all cheering]

124
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:48,890
I mean, come on. Forty years!
[chuckles] I mean, seriously, folks?

125
00:05:48,973 --> 00:05:50,391
[Vicki and Mark chuckle]

126
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:54,020
But, you know, a lot of people
probably don't know this...

127
00:05:54,103 --> 00:05:57,398
Mom and Dad, when they first got hitched,
did not have a honeymoon.

128
00:05:57,482 --> 00:05:59,192
-[crowd] Aww.
-Yeah. No honeymoon.

129
00:05:59,609 --> 00:06:01,235
-Sorry.
-They wanted to go to Hawaii,

130
00:06:01,319 --> 00:06:06,783
but instead, like they always did,
they sacrificed and pinched pennies,

131
00:06:06,866 --> 00:06:10,620
so they could provide a better life
for their family and their children.

132
00:06:11,913 --> 00:06:13,456
Well, Mom and Dad,

133
00:06:14,248 --> 00:06:16,334
I believe you've sacrificed enough.

134
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:17,543
[Hawaiian music playing]

135
00:06:21,130 --> 00:06:24,634
-[all] Aww!
-So, as an anniversary gift from me,

136
00:06:24,717 --> 00:06:28,012
Kelly, Nina and your future grandson,
of course,

137
00:06:28,096 --> 00:06:31,766
I think it is finally time
for you two to say aloha to Hawaii.

138
00:06:31,849 --> 00:06:33,309
-Oh!
-Yeah, you're going to Hawaii.

139
00:06:33,392 --> 00:06:34,602
-Oh!
-What?

140
00:06:34,685 --> 00:06:37,355
-[all cheering]
-Mom, Dad, get your butts up here!

141
00:06:37,855 --> 00:06:40,024
-We have a whole lei thing we want to do.
-[Mark] You're kidding, right?

142
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:41,442
-[Ken] No.
-[Vicki shouts, laughs]

143
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:43,653
-What's happening?
-He's sending them to Hawaii?

144
00:06:43,736 --> 00:06:45,071
[Andrew] Was there an e-mail chain
I missed?

145
00:06:45,154 --> 00:06:46,030
-[Caroline] No.
-No?

146
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:49,242
Oh, honey. Oh, thank you.

147
00:06:49,325 --> 00:06:50,409
[all] Aw!

148
00:06:50,493 --> 00:06:53,121
-What the fuck?
-Are you okay?

149
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:56,415
It's just this is a surprise to me, too.

150
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:58,000
Wait. He didn't tell you?

151
00:06:58,084 --> 00:07:00,044
It's fine. I mean,
we can barely pay our mortgage.

152
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,212
-But it's fine.
-Oh.

153
00:07:01,295 --> 00:07:04,715
-[Vicki laughing]
-Kelly! Kelly, come here.

154
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:06,300
[chuckles]

155
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:07,468
I'm sorry.

156
00:07:07,552 --> 00:07:10,847
-Come on, honey. Come on, honey. Let's...
-[Ken chuckles]

157
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:13,307
-[Ken] Does anyone have a camera?
-His stupid shoes.

158
00:07:13,391 --> 00:07:15,101
What a pig in shit.

159
00:07:15,184 --> 00:07:18,229
-This is too much. It's too much, Ken.
-Say aloha.

160
00:07:20,606 --> 00:07:24,193
-Wow, very thoughtful, Ken.
-Well, they deserve it.

161
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:25,736
Dude, what's wrong with you?

162
00:07:26,195 --> 00:07:29,490
What? No, I mean,
I wanted it to be a surprise, so...

163
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:31,325
You made us look like losers.

164
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:33,494
We could've pitched in
and given that together.

165
00:07:33,578 --> 00:07:36,873
But you guys spend your money
and travel here. That's your gift.

166
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:40,126
I live here, so this is my gift.
I didn't want to burden you.

167
00:07:40,209 --> 00:07:41,836
[Caroline] It's too big.

168
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:45,381
We should've done one of those
gift-from-the-kids kind of things.

169
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:49,385
Yeah. Like, when we got them TiVos.
It was, like, $13 each.

170
00:07:49,802 --> 00:07:52,180
Okay... Gus, back me up here.

171
00:07:52,263 --> 00:07:54,390
You know what I'm doing here.
It's just a nice gesture.

172
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:56,767
Yeah. No, it's very nice.

173
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:59,020
It's good,
but I see where they're coming from.

174
00:07:59,103 --> 00:08:00,855
-Really?
-A little bit, yeah.

175
00:08:00,938 --> 00:08:04,734
I thought you guys would be happy that
Mom and Dad finally get to go to Hawaii,

176
00:08:04,817 --> 00:08:06,444
but, all right,
just make it about yourselves.

177
00:08:06,527 --> 00:08:07,695
-Oh, my God.
-Oh, my God.

178
00:08:07,778 --> 00:08:09,363
You're such a dick, do you know that?

179
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:11,199
Oh, Andrew, we don't talk like that.

180
00:08:11,282 --> 00:08:13,451
-Okay, Drew, cut it.
-But he is a dick.

181
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:14,869
He didn't even tell us about this gift.

182
00:08:14,952 --> 00:08:17,330
We couldn't pitch in if we wanted to.

183
00:08:17,413 --> 00:08:19,790
I didn't want to make you feel stupid.
I was doing it as a surprise.

184
00:08:19,874 --> 00:08:21,042
Don't do this to me again. Stop it!

185
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:34,847
Well, uh, don't worry, Mom and Dad.
The three of us,

186
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:37,058
we actually chipped in for a present, too,
and um...

187
00:08:38,142 --> 00:08:40,269
we're gonna pay for your magazines
on the flight to Hawaii.

188
00:08:41,103 --> 00:08:44,357
But just on the flight there, okay,
not the flight back. We can't afford that.

189
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:48,945
-Oh! And we also got you this napkin.
-[Vicki] Oh.

190
00:08:49,445 --> 00:08:52,240
It's the paper napkin year, right?
Forty years, yeah?

191
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:53,491
Oh, who's this now?

192
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:58,746
Hey, I'm an old man with my white hair.
[chuckles]

193
00:08:59,413 --> 00:09:02,375
Hey, stop all this fightin' and fussin'.

194
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:06,671
Y'all sound like me and Hillary
after she found out about Monica.

195
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:11,467
I did not know
Ken was going to give that present.

196
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:13,010
[all laughing]

197
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:25,022
-So was I right or what?
-What?

198
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:27,483
-My family, I told you they're insane.
-[clicks tongue]

199
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:29,193
God. Did you see what Gus did?

200
00:09:29,277 --> 00:09:34,240
Like, every time shit gets weird,
he fuckin' turns into Jerry Seinfeld.

201
00:09:35,116 --> 00:09:39,579
Oh, he's really gotten super neurotic
since the whole Ridley Scott thing.

202
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:42,373
You guys talking about Ken's insane gift?

203
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:44,792
No, I was telling Mickey
about Ridley Scott.

204
00:09:44,875 --> 00:09:46,961
-Don't.
-What? It's not that big of a deal.

205
00:09:47,044 --> 00:09:49,672
Okay, I don't know
how much Gus has told you,

206
00:09:49,755 --> 00:09:52,258
but when he first got to LA,
he was hot shit.

207
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:53,843
-What?
-[Andrew] Yeah.

208
00:09:53,926 --> 00:09:55,261
-Really?
-Yeah. Totally.

209
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:58,055
He wrote this script that everyone saw,

210
00:09:58,139 --> 00:10:01,976
and he took all these cushy meetings
with important people.

211
00:10:02,059 --> 00:10:04,103
-Oh, okay.
-Yeah. It was nuts.

212
00:10:04,186 --> 00:10:06,897
And he got a job
as Ridley Scott's assistant,

213
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:10,484
but also to develop stuff with him.

214
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:11,569
-He was set.
-[chuckles]

215
00:10:11,652 --> 00:10:14,155
-Yeah, it was so promising.
-Yeah.

216
00:10:14,238 --> 00:10:16,657
Until... [chuckles softly]

217
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:19,910
Okay, so, I don't know what happened,
but he got in his head

218
00:10:19,994 --> 00:10:22,997
about his career not moving fast enough.

219
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:25,666
This is, like, a few months in only.

220
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:29,378
And so he sent Ridley
an e-mail saying, like,

221
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:33,799
"I need you to take me more seriously,"
and on and on and on.

222
00:10:33,883 --> 00:10:35,635
-Wait. Gus did that?
-Yeah.

223
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:37,637
That's ballsy. I like it.

224
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:43,768
But the e-mail also included
a long exchange he had with our mom,

225
00:10:43,851 --> 00:10:46,103
and it said how he should word it.

226
00:10:46,187 --> 00:10:50,066
He was asking her all these questions
about what he should say in the e-mail,

227
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:52,610
and that was all in there,
and the e-mail was just at the top.

228
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:54,153
-Uh-oh.
-It was... yeah.

229
00:10:54,236 --> 00:10:56,072
-Yeah. So...
-Oh.

230
00:10:56,155 --> 00:11:00,284
And, of course,
Ridley sends it to everyone he knows,

231
00:11:00,368 --> 00:11:05,206
like directors, agents, managers,
studio execs, and he's like,

232
00:11:05,289 --> 00:11:09,710
"Look what my little assistant sent me
from his mommy." [snickers]

233
00:11:10,544 --> 00:11:12,171
Did you guys see the e-mail?

234
00:11:12,254 --> 00:11:14,715
-Yeah, it's so bad. It's...
-It's awful.

235
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:17,218
At one point, he even says,
"Thanks, Mommy."

236
00:11:17,301 --> 00:11:18,386
-Like, yeah.
-No.

237
00:11:18,969 --> 00:11:20,596
[Andrew] Oh, my God. Mom's hammered.

238
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:24,141
I'm gonna give her the rest of my tequila
and see how fucked up she gets.

239
00:11:25,476 --> 00:11:26,560
Jesus!

240
00:11:27,478 --> 00:11:29,688
What? Last time she got hammered,

241
00:11:29,772 --> 00:11:32,733
