It was awesome.

242
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:34,527
You want to see that, right?

243
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,153
I'm gonna go get some cake.

244
00:11:36,779 --> 00:11:40,741
No, I don't want to see that.
That's, like, deeply sad.

245
00:11:42,993 --> 00:11:44,078
Uh...

246
00:11:44,703 --> 00:11:47,081
-"China Doll" by David Bowie.
-Very good.

247
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:50,000
-I'm cleaning up the cake.
-I see.

248
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:56,298
-[Vicki] Did you want a drink, honey?
-[Mark] No. Not right now.

249
00:11:56,382 --> 00:11:57,591
Okay.

250
00:11:57,675 --> 00:11:59,218
-Hey.
-Mmm.

251
00:11:59,301 --> 00:12:02,555
-How's it going? Everything okay?
-It's great. I'm having so much fun.

252
00:12:02,638 --> 00:12:05,474
-Why don't you come sit down?
-Oh, no, I'm good. This is my spot.

253
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:09,437
I can see everybody and look at...
Oh, there's Mickey! Hey, Mickey!

254
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:12,356
Get over here! There's my girl!

255
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:13,691
-Come here.
-Okay.

256
00:12:13,774 --> 00:12:17,069
You're my girl.
Come on over here.

257
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:18,612
Here she comes.

258
00:12:19,405 --> 00:12:21,449
Oh, Mickey, look at you.

259
00:12:22,032 --> 00:12:26,370
Mark and I were just talking,
and we decided that you're our favorite.

260
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:28,247
-Oh, no.
-[Mark] That's true.

261
00:12:28,831 --> 00:12:30,040
It's very sweet of you.

262
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:34,295
Of all the girls that Gussie brought home,
you are number one best.

263
00:12:34,378 --> 00:12:37,631
Really, so much better than that...
What's her name? Natalie.

264
00:12:37,715 --> 00:12:41,427
-Boom. Shots fired, Natalie.
-Well, Natalie was a bitch.

265
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:43,512
-Let's just admit it.
-Hey, oh. [chuckles]

266
00:12:43,596 --> 00:12:47,266
You know, I mean, I could tell, Gussie.
Moms always can tell.

267
00:12:47,349 --> 00:12:51,145
-Okay, Vicks, let's take it easy.
-Who else was there? Um... Uh...

268
00:12:51,228 --> 00:12:54,273
-Who else was there? Theresa. [buzzes]
-Yes.

269
00:12:54,356 --> 00:12:56,650
-Am I right? [buzzes]
-I don't know about that.

270
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:59,069
That seems like an oversimplification.
[chuckles]

271
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:02,740
Come on. The thing about Theresa was,
she was just boring.

272
00:13:02,823 --> 00:13:04,366
-Hmm.
-You'd say to her,

273
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:06,869
"Oh, so, where are you from?"

274
00:13:06,952 --> 00:13:10,915
And she'd say, "Lansing."
Or wherever. And that was it.

275
00:13:10,998 --> 00:13:12,166
-[Mickey] Hmm.
-Um...

276
00:13:12,249 --> 00:13:15,044
-Excuse me, but are you an alien?
-[all laugh]

277
00:13:15,127 --> 00:13:17,087
-You know?
-Yeah, well, it's true.

278
00:13:17,171 --> 00:13:19,673
-Mickey's the very best.
-She's the number one best.

279
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:22,218
The number one.
You have to grab on to this one.

280
00:13:22,301 --> 00:13:24,637
-This is the one to hold on to.
-I will.

281
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,971
I'm not letting her go!

282
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:27,806
[Mark] My dad is leaving.
We should probably go say goodbye.

283
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:31,143
[Vicki] Sure, let's go say bye to Daddy.
Here we go.

284
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:40,110
[Mickey] Excuse me. I'm sorry.

285
00:13:45,741 --> 00:13:47,701
-Fuck this.
-[Gus] Hey.

286
00:13:48,994 --> 00:13:49,828
Where you goin'?

287
00:13:49,912 --> 00:13:51,330
-Going to the airport.
-Mickey, where you going?

288
00:13:51,413 --> 00:13:53,958
-Come on.
-I'm going to the airport!

289
00:13:54,041 --> 00:13:56,961
You lie to me so much.
I know about the whole Ridley Scott thing.

290
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:59,964
Okay, look. It was late at night,
all right?

291
00:14:00,047 --> 00:14:01,841
I wasn't keeping track
of my e-mails. It was very confusing.

292
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:03,467
I was forwarding stuff and was confused!

293
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:05,761
Dude! Why wouldn't you tell me that?

294
00:14:06,971 --> 00:14:09,723
'Cause it's not a great seduction story,
Mickey, okay?

295
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:11,308
On our first date, I'm not gonna go,

296
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:14,061
"Hey. Just so you know,
I embarrassed myself in front of

297
00:14:14,144 --> 00:14:16,146
-half of--"
-Give me the keys.

298
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:19,149
-Wait. You're just going to take the...
-Yeah.

299
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:20,484
Give me the keys.

300
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:23,863
-Thank--
-No.

301
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:25,030
What? Are you serious?

302
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:26,615
-Give me the keys.
-I don't want to--

303
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:28,867
-[stammers] Give me the key!
-Stop it.

304
00:14:28,951 --> 00:14:30,911
[hisses] Gus.

305
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:34,456
You think that I'm not ready
to be a mother,

306
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:36,750
but you behave like a little baby.

307
00:14:36,834 --> 00:14:38,085
You've got all these lies,

308
00:14:38,168 --> 00:14:40,421
and you run and you hide,
and you keep secrets.

309
00:14:40,504 --> 00:14:43,132
You were engaged.
The whole Ridley Scott thing.

310
00:14:43,215 --> 00:14:45,342
And you tell your parents
you go to church?

311
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:47,011
You're making it sound worse than it is.

312
00:14:47,094 --> 00:14:50,222
I'm just trying
to make people happy. Okay?

313
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:52,099
So I lie and hide a little bit.

314
00:14:52,182 --> 00:14:55,269
I don't think there's anything super wrong
with that, Mickey.

315
00:14:56,312 --> 00:14:58,063
It's your whole family.

316
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:00,566
Yeah, my family's nuts,
but we put it all out there.

317
00:15:00,649 --> 00:15:04,111
You don't even know my family, okay?
They're way deeper than that.

318
00:15:04,194 --> 00:15:08,866
You can't just come in and, like, "Oh,
two days, I sum up your whole family."

319
00:15:08,949 --> 00:15:10,367
Maybe I didn't want you to come with me,

320
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:12,703
and it had nothing to do
with me and my family, okay?

321
00:15:15,122 --> 00:15:17,124
-It's me? Is that what you're saying?
-Yeah, maybe.

322
00:15:17,207 --> 00:15:19,418
Maybe it was you. Maybe I didn't want
to bring you because you,

323
00:15:19,501 --> 00:15:21,420
not because of me,
not because of my family,

324
00:15:21,503 --> 00:15:23,380
not because we're keeping secrets.

325
00:15:23,464 --> 00:15:27,343
Or whatever Eugene O'Neill drama
you have in your head right now.

326
00:15:27,426 --> 00:15:29,595
All right. Cool.

327
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,514
Yeah, I'm gonna go.

328
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:38,520
Go. I don't care.

329
00:15:40,439 --> 00:15:44,693
Can you just go in and say goodbye
to everybody?

330
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:47,905
Just make up an excuse or something,
so I don't have to feel stupid.

331
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:50,908
Yeah, I can do that.

332
00:15:59,792 --> 00:16:01,377
I just need a minute, okay?

333
00:16:17,017 --> 00:16:18,978
Uh... Hey, everybody...

334
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:22,731
Sorry, bad news,
but Mickey's gotta leave town

335
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:24,358
and go to the airport now.

336
00:16:24,983 --> 00:16:25,901
